lessons.body:
Zod Resolver & Shared Validation
Rules
Reuse rules without confusing form, transport and persistence contracts

Phase 21 - Forms with React Hook Form + Zod
Volume 06 - Professional Frontend

Why Zod appears again
NestJS already validates transport input with Zod. The frontend also needs immediate validation
feedback. This is the first time the same field-level rules are genuinely useful in two workspace
packages, so a small shared validators package has now earned its place.

packages/validators: reusable field primitives

apps/api: HTTP transport schema

apps/web: UI form schema

Both use Zod 4.6.5

Shared field primitives
// packages/validators/src/tasks.ts
import { z } from "zod";

export const taskTitleSchema = z
.string()
.trim()
.min(1, "Title is required.")
.max(200, "Title must be 200 characters or fewer.");

export const taskDescriptionSchema = z
.string()
.trim()
.max(2000, "Description must be 2000 characters or fewer.");

export const taskPrioritySchema = z.enum([
"LOW", "MEDIUM", "HIGH",
]);

UI form schema

// apps/web/src/components/tasks/task-form.schema.ts
import { z } from "zod";
import {
taskDescriptionSchema,
taskPrioritySchema,
taskTitleSchema,
} from "@taskflow/validators/tasks";

export const taskFormSchema = z.object({
title: taskTitleSchema,
description: taskDescriptionSchema,
priority: taskPrioritySchema,
dueAtLocal: z.string(),
});

export type TaskFormValues = z.infer<typeof taskFormSchema>;

Connect Zod to React Hook Form
const form = useForm<TaskFormValues>({
resolver: zodResolver(taskFormSchema),
defaultValues,
mode: "onBlur",
});

Important boundary

The UI form schema is allowed to differ from the API transport schema. For example, an HTML datetime-local
value is a local string; the API may require an ISO timestamp. Map between them deliberately on submit.

Why not share the Prisma model?
A Prisma model describes persistence. A form schema describes editing. A transport schema describes
an HTTP request. They overlap, but they are not interchangeable contracts.

