Create Task Form - End to End
Build the first real browser form against the secured NestJS API

Phase 21 - Forms with React Hook Form + Zod
Volume 06 - Professional Frontend

Build CreateTaskForm
The create form starts with empty defaults, validates locally, maps UI values to the API contract,
acquires a current Supabase access token, submits to NestJS, and then refreshes the Task list after
success.

const defaultValues: TaskFormValues = {
title: "",
description: "",
priority: "MEDIUM",
dueAtLocal: "",
};

Map UI values to API input
function toCreateTaskInput(
projectId: string,
values: TaskFormValues,
) {
return {
projectId,
title: values.title,
description: values.description || null,
priority: values.priority,
dueAt: values.dueAtLocal
? new Date(values.dueAtLocal).toISOString()
: null,
};
}

Submission
const onSubmit = handleSubmit(async (values) => {
clearErrors("root.server");

try {
const input = toCreateTaskInput(projectId, values);
await createTaskFromBrowser(input);
reset(defaultValues);
router.push("/tasks");
router.refresh();
} catch (error) {
setError("root.server", {
message: messageForApiError(error),
});
}
});

User edits form

zodResolver validates UI shape

Map local values -> API input

Browser sends Bearer token + JSON

NestJS validates again

Authorization + business rules

PostgreSQL accepts / rejects

UI handles authoritative result

Prevent duplicate submissions
Use isSubmitting to disable the submit button while the promise returned by the submit handler is
pending. Do not maintain a second manual loading flag for the same form operation unless it
represents different state.

<button type="submit" disabled={isSubmitting}>
{isSubmitting ? "Creating..." : "Create task"}
</button>

